# Simulated IR brightness temperature (KELVIN) — classic enhanced-IR look:
# warm ground in grayscale (dark = hot), cold convective tops through the
# cyan/green/yellow/red/magenta/white ladder. Fully opaque like real
# satellite imagery.
#
# ⚠ Keyed in KELVIN, verified empirically 2026-08-05: the first render
# with Celsius stops came out single-color (every pixel clamped to the
# hottest stop) — GDAL's K->C normalization applies to TMP fields like
# t2m but NOT to SBT brightness temperatures, which arrive raw in K.
